    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0499" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/24: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-13T15:00:00+08:00">December 13, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 13—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1142. Japanese Consulate General informs us by telephone that large seaplane will
                    leave early tomorrow morning and land on river <pb facs="0500" n="492"
                        xml:id="pg492"/> in vicinity of Hohsien. Plane is to carry doctors, nurses
                    and medical supplies.</p>
                <p>Sent to Hankow, repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
